{"title":"Data Analyst Roadmap","role":"Data Analyst","summary":"A Data Analyst collects, cleans, analyzes, and interprets data to help organizations make better decisions.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Engineering Physics"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Data Analyst collects, cleans, analyzes, and interprets data to help organizations make better decisions."},{"type":"p","text":"For an Engineering Physics graduate, the combination can be particularly strong because the degree develops mathematical modeling, quantitative reasoning, physics-based problem solving, programming, statistics, and experimental analysis."},{"type":"p","text":"The student can build a profile around:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Engineering Physics","Statistics","Programming","Data Analytics","Domain Analytics"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Typical responsibilities include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Data collection and cleaning"},{"text":"Exploratory data analysis"},{"text":"Statistical analysis"},{"text":"Dashboard development"},{"text":"KPI reporting"},{"text":"Trend identification"},{"text":"Forecasting"},{"text":"Experiment analysis"},{"text":"Business/technical reporting"},{"text":"Data-driven decision support"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Career Stage","Possible Roles","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Entry Level"},{"text":"Data Analyst, Junior Data Analyst, Reporting Analyst"},{"text":"Data preparation & reporting"}],[{"text":"2–4 Years"},{"text":"Data Analyst, Business/Data Analyst, Product Analyst"},{"text":"Advanced analytics"}],[{"text":"4–7 Years"},{"text":"Senior Data Analyst, Analytics Consultant, Data Analytics Lead"},{"text":"Decision support"}],[{"text":"7–12 Years"},{"text":"Analytics Manager, Data Science Manager, Analytics Consultant"},{"text":"Analytics strategy"}],[{"text":"12+ Years"},{"text":"Head of Analytics, Director of Data & Analytics"},{"text":"Enterprise analytics"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During B.Tech","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The ideal development path is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Engineering Physics","Mathematics & Statistics","Programming","SQL & Databases","Data Cleaning","Exploratory Data Analysis","Visualization & BI","Statistical Modeling","Domain Analytics"]},{"type":"p","text":"The degree already provides strong quantitative foundations. The main objective is to deliberately build the data-analysis toolkit alongside the physics curriculum."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Mathematics, Physics & Programming"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong foundations in:"},{"type":"h","text":"Mathematics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Calculus"},{"text":"Linear algebra"},{"text":"Differential equations"},{"text":"Probability"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Numerical methods"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Physics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Classical mechanics"},{"text":"Electromagnetism"},{"text":"Thermodynamics"},{"text":"Quantum physics fundamentals"},{"text":"Experimental physics"},{"text":"These subjects strengthen analytical thinking and quantitative modeling."}]}]},{"heading":"Programming Foundation","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Start with:"},{"type":"h","text":"Python"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Variables"},{"text":"Functions"},{"text":"Data structures"},{"text":"File handling"},{"text":"Exception handling"},{"text":"Object-oriented basics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Then move toward:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"NumPy"},{"text":"pandas"},{"text":"matplotlib"}]},{"type":"h","text":"SQL"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn early:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SELECT"},{"text":"WHERE"},{"text":"GROUP BY"},{"text":"ORDER BY"},{"text":"JOIN"},{"text":"CASE"},{"text":"Aggregate functions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Later add:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Subqueries"},{"text":"CTEs"},{"text":"Window functions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1–2 — Statistics for Data Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Statistics is one of the most important bridges between Engineering Physics and Data Analytics."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"h","text":"Descriptive Statistics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mean"},{"text":"Median"},{"text":"Mode"},{"text":"Variance"},{"text":"Standard deviation"},{"text":"Percentiles"},{"text":"Distribution analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Probability"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Conditional probability"},{"text":"Bayes' theorem"},{"text":"Random variables"},{"text":"Probability distributions"},{"text":"Expected value"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Statistical Inference"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Confidence intervals"},{"text":"Hypothesis testing"},{"text":"p-values"},{"text":"Statistical significance"}]}]},{"heading":"Experimental Data Analysis","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Engineering Physics provides an advantage in analyzing experimental datasets."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Measurement uncertainty"},{"text":"Error propagation"},{"text":"Experimental design"},{"text":"Regression"},{"text":"Correlation"},{"text":"Outlier analysis"},{"text":"Calibration"},{"text":"Reproducibility"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the difference between:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Correlation","Association","Causation"]},{"type":"p","text":"and avoid drawing causal conclusions from observational data without appropriate evidence."}]},{"heading":"Year 2 — Data Cleaning & Preparation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Real-world analytics involves substantial data preparation."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to handle:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Missing values"},{"text":"Duplicate records"},{"text":"Incorrect data types"},{"text":"Outliers"},{"text":"Inconsistent categories"},{"text":"Date/time data"},{"text":"Data validation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"pandas Skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Become comfortable with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"read_csv"},{"text":"read_excel"},{"text":"filtering"},{"text":"grouping"},{"text":"merging"},{"text":"reshaping"},{"text":"aggregation"},{"text":"datetime operations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Typical workflow:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Raw Data","Data Quality Check","Cleaning","Transformation","Validation","Analysis"]}]},{"heading":"Year 2 — Excel","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Become highly proficient in Excel."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"XLOOKUP"},{"text":"INDEX/MATCH"},{"text":"SUMIFS"},{"text":"COUNTIFS"},{"text":"IF/IFS"},{"text":"Pivot Tables"},{"text":"Charts"},{"text":"Conditional formatting"},{"text":"Data validation"},{"text":"Power Query"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Then move to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Scenario analysis"},{"text":"Forecasting"},{"text":"Solver"},{"text":"Dashboard development"},{"text":"Excel remains useful for business-facing analytics even when Python and SQL are available."}]}]},{"heading":"SQL for Data Analysts","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Build SQL skills beyond basic querying."},{"type":"h","text":"Core"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SELECT"},{"text":"FROM"},{"text":"WHERE"},{"text":"GROUP BY"},{"text":"HAVING"},{"text":"ORDER BY"},{"text":"JOIN"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Intermediate"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Subqueries"},{"text":"CTEs"},{"text":"CASE statements"},{"text":"Date functions"},{"text":"String functions"},{"text":"Window functions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Analytical SQL"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to calculate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Running totals"},{"text":"Ranking"},{"text":"Moving averages"},{"text":"Retention"},{"text":"Conversion rates"},{"text":"Year-over-year growth"},{"text":"Month-over-month growth"}]}]},{"heading":"Year 2–3 — Data Visualization","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn how to communicate data effectively."},{"type":"h","text":"Power BI"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop dashboards for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sales"},{"text":"Finance"},{"text":"Operations"},{"text":"Marketing"},{"text":"Customer analytics"},{"text":"Product performance"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Data modeling"},{"text":"Relationships"},{"text":"DAX fundamentals"},{"text":"Measures"},{"text":"Filters"},{"text":"Drill-through"},{"text":"Interactive reports"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Visualization Principles"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to select appropriate charts rather than simply making visually complex dashboards."}]},{"heading":"Exploratory Data Analysis","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop a structured EDA process:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Business / Research Question","Understand Dataset","Data Quality Check","Univariate Analysis","Bivariate / Multivariate Analysis","Identify Patterns","Test Hypotheses","Generate Insights"]},{"type":"p","text":"Look for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Trends"},{"text":"Seasonality"},{"text":"Relationships"},{"text":"Outliers"},{"text":"Segments"},{"text":"Anomalies"}]}]},{"heading":"Year 3 — Statistical Modeling","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn practical statistical methods."},{"type":"h","text":"Regression"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Linear regression"},{"text":"Multiple regression"},{"text":"Logistic regression"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Other Methods"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Correlation analysis"},{"text":"ANOVA fundamentals"},{"text":"Time-series analysis"},{"text":"Clustering"},{"text":"Hypothesis testing"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on understanding:"},{"type":"flow","items":["used?","What assumptions does it make?","How should the result be interpreted?"],"label":"When should a method be"}]},{"heading":"Python for Data Analytics","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop an analytics stack:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Python"},{"text":"├── NumPy"},{"text":"├── pandas"},{"text":"├── SciPy"},{"text":"├── matplotlib"},{"text":"├── seaborn"},{"text":"└── scikit-learn"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Use Python for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Data cleaning"},{"text":"Statistical analysis"},{"text":"Visualization"},{"text":"Regression"},{"text":"Forecasting"},{"text":"Automation"},{"text":"Basic machine learning"}]}]},{"heading":"Engineering Physics + Data Analytics Advantage","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The specialization can be used to develop domain-specific analytics rather than competing only for generic business analyst positions."},{"type":"p","text":"Potential areas include:"},{"type":"h","text":"Scientific Data"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Experimental data"},{"text":"Laboratory measurements"},{"text":"Sensor data"},{"text":"Instrumentation data"},{"text":"Simulation results"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Engineering Analytics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Manufacturing"},{"text":"Energy"},{"text":"Electronics"},{"text":"Semiconductor"},{"text":"Materials"},{"text":"Aerospace"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Product analytics"},{"text":"IoT analytics"},{"text":"Sensor analytics"},{"text":"Reliability analytics"},{"text":"This can create a differentiated profile."}]}]},{"heading":"Year 3 — Time-Series Analysis","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Engineering and scientific systems often generate time-dependent data."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Time-series decomposition"},{"text":"Trend"},{"text":"Seasonality"},{"text":"Moving averages"},{"text":"Exponential smoothing"},{"text":"Autocorrelation"},{"text":"ARIMA fundamentals"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Applications:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Energy consumption"},{"text":"Sensor monitoring"},{"text":"Equipment performance"},{"text":"Production"},{"text":"Demand forecasting"},{"text":"Environmental data"}]}]},{"heading":"Data Quality & Statistical Thinking","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong Data Analyst should understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sampling bias"},{"text":"Selection bias"},{"text":"Measurement error"},{"text":"Missing-data mechanisms"},{"text":"Confounding"},{"text":"Data leakage"},{"text":"Outliers"},{"text":"Simpson's paradox"},{"text":"Multiple comparisons"},{"text":"This is especially useful for an Engineering Physics graduate because scientific training can strengthen experimental reasoning."}]}]},{"heading":"Year 3–4 — Business Analytics","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"To become employable as a general Data Analyst, add business knowledge."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"h","text":"Business Metrics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Revenue"},{"text":"Profit"},{"text":"Conversion rate"},{"text":"Customer acquisition cost"},{"text":"Customer retention"},{"text":"Churn"},{"text":"Average order value"},{"text":"Operational efficiency"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Product Analytics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"DAU/MAU"},{"text":"Funnel analysis"},{"text":"Cohort analysis"},{"text":"Retention"},{"text":"Feature adoption"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Operations Analytics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Productivity"},{"text":"Cost"},{"text":"Quality"},{"text":"Inventory"},{"text":"Capacity"},{"text":"Delivery performance"}]}]},{"heading":"Data Storytelling","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Data Analyst should not simply provide numbers."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to communicate:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Data","Observation","Insight","Business / Technical Meaning","Recommendation","Expected Impact"]},{"type":"p","text":"For every dashboard or analysis, ask:"},{"type":"h","text":"“What decision should this analysis help someone make?”"}]},{"heading":"Advanced Analytics","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"After mastering core analytics, optionally develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Machine learning"},{"text":"Classification"},{"text":"Regression"},{"text":"Clustering"},{"text":"Anomaly detection"},{"text":"Feature engineering"},{"text":"Model evaluation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Important libraries:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"scikit-learn"},{"text":"SciPy"},{"text":"XGBoost fundamentals"},{"text":"Machine learning should complement, not replace, strong SQL, statistics, and data-cleaning skills."}]}]},{"heading":"Engineering & Scientific Analytics Specializations","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Engineering Physics graduate can specialize in:"},{"type":"h","text":"Energy Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyze:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Energy consumption"},{"text":"Renewable generation"},{"text":"Energy efficiency"},{"text":"Demand forecasting"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semiconductor Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyze:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Process data"},{"text":"Yield"},{"text":"Defects"},{"text":"Equipment performance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Manufacturing Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyze:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Production"},{"text":"Quality"},{"text":"Downtime"},{"text":"OEE"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Scientific Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyze:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Experimental data"},{"text":"Research datasets"},{"text":"Sensor measurements"},{"text":"Simulation outputs"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Materials Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyze:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Material properties"},{"text":"Characterization data"},{"text":"Experimental results"}]}]},{"heading":"Final-Year Project Ideas","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Energy Consumption Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyze electricity consumption and build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Python analysis"},{"text":"SQL database"},{"text":"Power BI dashboard"},{"text":"Demand forecast"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Scientific Experiment Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a system to analyze experimental measurements and identify:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Trends"},{"text":"Outliers"},{"text":"Uncertainty"},{"text":"Statistical relationships"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Predictive Maintenance Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Use sensor data to identify potential equipment failures."},{"type":"p","text":"Workflow:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Sensor Data","Data Cleaning","Feature Engineering","Anomaly Detection","Failure Prediction","Maintenance Recommendation"]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — Semiconductor Yield Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyze production data to identify factors associated with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Defects"},{"text":"Yield loss"},{"text":"Process variation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — Materials Property Prediction"},{"type":"p","text":"Use experimental/material datasets to predict:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Strength"},{"text":"Conductivity"},{"text":"Thermal properties"},{"text":"Other material characteristics"}]}]},{"heading":"Internship Strategy","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Target internships in:"},{"type":"h","text":"Analytics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Data Analytics"},{"text":"Business Analytics"},{"text":"Operations Analytics"},{"text":"Product Analytics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Engineering"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Manufacturing analytics"},{"text":"Semiconductor analytics"},{"text":"Energy analytics"},{"text":"Quality analytics"},{"text":"Reliability analytics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Scientific computing"},{"text":"Experimental data analysis"},{"text":"Computational physics"},{"text":"Research data management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Internship Responsibilities"},{"type":"p","text":"Prioritize roles involving:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Statistical analysis"},{"text":"Data cleaning"},{"text":"Dashboard development"},{"text":"Forecasting"},{"text":"Experimental data analysis"}]}]},{"heading":"Entry-Level Career Options","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"After B.Tech, suitable roles include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Data Analyst"},{"text":"Junior Data Analyst"},{"text":"Business Data Analyst"},{"text":"Operations Analyst"},{"text":"Reporting Analyst"},{"text":"BI Analyst"},{"text":"Product Data Analyst"},{"text":"Research Data Analyst"},{"text":"Scientific Data Analyst"},{"text":"Energy Data Analyst"},{"text":"Engineering Data Analyst"},{"text":"Quality Data Analyst"}]}]},{"heading":"Employer Skill Matrix","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Employer Type","High-Value Skills"],"rows":[[{"text":"IT Services"},{"text":"SQL + Python + BI"}],[{"text":"Product Companies"},{"text":"SQL + Product Analytics"}],[{"text":"Manufacturing"},{"text":"Statistics + Operations Analytics"}],[{"text":"Semiconductor"},{"text":"Engineering + Data Analytics"}],[{"text":"Energy"},{"text":"Time Series + Energy Analytics"}],[{"text":"Consulting"},{"text":"Analytics + Business Communication"}],[{"text":"Research Organizations"},{"text":"Statistics + Scientific Computing"}],[{"text":"E-commerce"},{"text":"SQL + Customer Analytics"}],[{"text":"Finance"},{"text":"Statistics + SQL + Business Analytics"}],[{"text":"Healthcare"},{"text":"Statistics + Data Quality"}]]}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"High Priority"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Advanced Excel"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Python for Data Analysis"},{"text":"Statistics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Useful"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Google/IBM/Microsoft-oriented data analytics programs"},{"text":"Tableau"},{"text":"Cloud fundamentals"},{"text":"Business analytics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Machine learning"},{"text":"Advanced SQL"},{"text":"Data engineering fundamentals"},{"text":"Experimentation/A-B testing"},{"text":"Time-series forecasting"},{"text":"The student should prioritize projects and demonstrable analytical ability over accumulating certificates."}]}]},{"heading":"PG Options","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A B.Tech Engineering Physics graduate has several possible postgraduate directions."},{"type":"h","text":"Technical"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Tech / M.E. Engineering Physics"},{"text":"Applied Physics"},{"text":"Computational Science"},{"text":"Data Science"},{"text":"Artificial Intelligence"},{"text":"Computational Engineering"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Analytics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MS Data Science"},{"text":"MS Business Analytics"},{"text":"MS Statistics"},{"text":"MS Applied Mathematics"},{"text":"MS Computational Science"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Specialized"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Computational Physics"},{"text":"Scientific Computing"},{"text":"Materials Science"},{"text":"Energy Systems"},{"text":"Semiconductor Technology"},{"text":"A PG in Data Science or Analytics is optional for entering Data Analytics; a strong portfolio can be sufficient for many entry-level roles."}]}]},{"heading":"Career Specializations","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"1. Business Data Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyze business performance and support management decisions."},{"type":"h","text":"2. Product Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyze customer behavior and product performance."},{"type":"h","text":"3. Engineering Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Use engineering knowledge to analyze technical systems."},{"type":"h","text":"4. Scientific Data Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Work with experimental and research datasets."},{"type":"h","text":"5. Energy Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyze energy systems, demand, and efficiency."},{"type":"h","text":"6. Manufacturing Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Optimize production and quality."},{"type":"h","text":"7. Semiconductor Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyze process, yield, and equipment data."},{"type":"h","text":"8. Data Science"},{"type":"p","text":"Progress toward predictive modeling and machine learning."}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"General Analytics Path"},{"type":"flow","items":["Data Analyst","Senior Data Analyst","Analytics Lead","Analytics Manager","Senior Analytics Manager","Head of Analytics","Director of Data & Analytics"]},{"type":"h","text":"Technical Path"},{"type":"flow","items":["Data Analyst","Advanced Data Analyst","Data Scientist / Analytics Engineer","Senior Data Scientist","Principal / Lead"]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact transition depends on the student's development in statistics, programming, machine learning, and data engineering."}]},{"heading":"Emerging Technologies","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The future Data Analyst should understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Generative AI for analytics"},{"text":"Natural-language querying"},{"text":"AI-assisted SQL"},{"text":"Automated data preparation"},{"text":"Augmented analytics"},{"text":"Real-time analytics"},{"text":"Data observability"},{"text":"Synthetic data"},{"text":"Causal inference"},{"text":"Automated forecasting"},{"text":"Semantic data layers"},{"text":"Modern cloud data platforms"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Engineering Physics Advantage"},{"type":"p","text":"The student can combine these with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Scientific computing"},{"text":"Sensor analytics"},{"text":"Digital twins"},{"text":"Simulation data"},{"text":"Engineering AI"},{"text":"Scientific machine learning"}]}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"DATA ANALYTICS"},{"text":"├── Data Cleaning"},{"text":"├── EDA"},{"text":"├── Statistical Analysis"},{"text":"├── Visualization"},{"text":"└── Data Storytelling"},{"text":"PROGRAMMING"},{"text":"├── Python"},{"text":"├── NumPy"},{"text":"├── pandas"},{"text":"├── SciPy"},{"text":"└── scikit-learn"},{"text":"DATABASE"},{"text":"├── SQL"},{"text":"├── Joins"},{"text":"├── CTEs"},{"text":"├── Window Functions"},{"text":"└── Data Modeling"},{"text":"BI"},{"text":"├── Power BI"},{"text":"├── DAX Fundamentals"},{"text":"├── Power Query"},{"text":"└── Dashboard Design"},{"text":"STATISTICS"},{"text":"├── Probability"},{"text":"├── Hypothesis Testing"},{"text":"├── Regression"},{"text":"├── Experimental Design"},{"text":"└── Time Series"},{"text":"ENGINEERING ANALYTICS"},{"text":"├── Sensor Data"},{"text":"├── Experimental Data"},{"text":"├── Simulation Data"},{"text":"├── Reliability"},{"text":"└── Scientific Computing"},{"text":"BUSINESS"},{"text":"├── KPIs"},{"text":"├── Business Metrics"},{"text":"├── Problem Framing"},{"text":"└── Decision Support"}]}]},{"heading":"Target Profile by Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, the student should be able to take a raw dataset and independently execute:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Question","Data","Cleaning","Analysis","Visualization","Insight","Recommendation"]},{"type":"p","text":"The student should be capable of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Writing intermediate-to-advanced SQL"},{"text":"Cleaning datasets using Python/pandas"},{"text":"Performing statistical analysis"},{"text":"Building professional Power BI dashboards"},{"text":"Conducting exploratory data analysis"},{"text":"Applying regression and basic forecasting"},{"text":"Explaining statistical results"},{"text":"Automating repetitive analytical tasks"},{"text":"Presenting insights to technical and non-technical stakeholders"},{"text":"Building 3–5 substantial analytics projects"},{"text":"A particularly strong profile would contain at least one domain-specific project connecting Engineering Physics with analytics."}]}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"“Data Analyst with strong quantitative foundations in Engineering Physics, specializing in statistical analysis, Python/SQL, business intelligence, and engineering/scientific data analytics.”"},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest strategy for this degree is not to abandon the Engineering Physics background and compete only as a generic Data Analyst. Instead, use the quantitative and scientific foundation as a differentiator."},{"type":"p","text":"The combination of Engineering Physics + Statistics + Python + SQL + Power BI + domain analytics can open pathways into technology, manufacturing, semiconductor, energy, scientific research, engineering, product analytics, and eventually Data Science."}]}]}